**Nuclear eccentricity did not change consistently with Oxaliplatin 10 µM.**

We quantified nuclear eccentricity in [Cell line] cells ([treatment and duration]) labelled with [antibody or dye for each stain]. Small dots show individual nuclei, coloured by run; large symbols show the value of each run (the mean of its fields, each field summarised by the median of its nuclei); lines join the same run; grey outlines show the distribution of nuclei; horizontal lines show the mean of runs. n = 3 runs per condition; 51 (Untreated) and 47 (Oxaliplatin 10 µM) nuclei from 9 fields per condition; individual nuclei and fields are not treated as independent replicates. Per-run differences (Oxaliplatin 10 µM − Untreated): −0.034 (Rep1), −0.054 (Rep2) and +0.028 (Rep3). No hypothesis test or confidence interval was calculated because the independence of the runs was not confirmed. Not shown: 53 nuclei without a value for this measure (listed in the source tables).
